============================================================
1. GENERAL PRINCIPLES
============================================================
- Consistency over cleverness
- Readability over brevity
- Explicit over implicit
- Pure functions over side effects
- Composition over inheritance
- Fail fast, fail loudly
- Small components, small modules
- One responsibility per file


============================================================
2. NAMING CONVENTIONS
============================================================

FILES & FOLDERS
---------------
React components: PascalCase (EventDetail.jsx)
React hooks: camelCase starting with "use" (useEvents.js)
React pages: PascalCase (MemberDashboard.jsx)
Feature folders: lowercase (events, programs, admin)
API modules: camelCase ending with Api (eventsApi.js)
FastAPI routers: snake_case (events_router.py)
FastAPI models: PascalCase (EventCreate, UserOut)
Database tables: snake_case (event_volunteers)
Database columns: snake_case (created_at)
Celery tasks: snake_case (send_email_task)

VARIABLES
---------
JavaScript: camelCase (eventList, userProfile)
Python: snake_case (event_list, user_profile)
Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE (MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE)
React state: camelCase (isLoading, errorMessage)

COMPONENTS
----------
Components: nouns (EventCard, MemberProfile)
Hooks: verbs (useEvents, useVoting)
Pages: match route names (AdminEvents.jsx)


============================================================
3. REACT STANDARDS
============================================================

COMPONENT TYPES
---------------
UI Components: Pure, reusable, no business logic
Feature Components: Domain-specific logic, API calls allowed
Page Components: Route-level, thin wrappers, no logic
Layout Components: Navigation, structure, role-aware menus

COMPONENT RULES
---------------
- One component per file
- Max 200 lines per component
- No inline styles
- No business logic in pages
- No API calls in layout components
- No global state except auth/theme

HOOKS
-----
- All data fetching must use hooks
- Hooks return { data, isLoading, error, refetch }
- Hooks do not render UI
- Hooks do not mutate global state

STATE MANAGEMENT
----------------
Global: Auth, roles, theme
Feature: useEvents, usePrograms, useMembers
Local: Form inputs, toggles, pagination

ERROR & LOADING HANDLING
------------------------
Pages handle loading/error states
Feature components do not render spinners
Use <LoadingSpinner /> and <ErrorMessage />


============================================================
4. FASTAPI STANDARDS
============================================================

PROJECT STRUCTURE
-----------------
/app
  /routers
  /models
  /schemas
  /services
  /db
  /auth
  /tasks
  main.py

ROUTERS
-------
- One router per domain
- Prefix matches API spec (/api/events)
- Tags match domain ("Events")
- No business logic in routers

SERVICES
--------
- All business logic in services/
- Services are pure functions
- Services do not return ORM objects

SCHEMAS (PYDANTIC)
------------------
- Separate Create, Update, Out schemas
- No ORM models in responses
- Use alias_generator for camelCase → snake_case

ORM (SQLALCHEMY)
----------------
- One model per file
- Use declarative base
- Use relationship() sparingly
- No cascading deletes unless required

ERROR HANDLING
--------------
- Use HTTPException for API errors
- Use custom exceptions for business logic
- Log all errors with context


============================================================
5. DATABASE STANDARDS (POSTGRES)
============================================================

SCHEMA RULES
------------
snake_case for tables & columns
id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY
created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()
updated_at TIMESTAMP (manual update)
FKs specify ON DELETE behavior

RELATIONSHIP RULES
------------------
One-to-many: FK on child table
Many-to-many: join table
Never store arrays of IDs

INDEXING
--------
Index all foreign keys
Index frequently queried columns
Use composite indexes for multi-column filters


============================================================
6. API STANDARDS
============================================================

REST RULES
----------
GET: Retrieve
POST: Create
PUT: Replace entire resource
PATCH: Partial update
DELETE: Remove resource

RESPONSE FORMAT
---------------
{
  "success": true,
  "data": { ... },
  "error": null
}

ERROR FORMAT
------------
{
  "success": false,
  "error": {
    "code": "EVENT_NOT_FOUND",
    "message": "Event does not exist"
  }
}

AUTHENTICATION
--------------
JWT access tokens
httpOnly cookies
Roles embedded in token


============================================================
7. CELERY STANDARDS
============================================================

TASK RULES
----------
Tasks must be idempotent
Tasks must log start/end
Tasks must use retry policies
Tasks must not block

QUEUE NAMING
------------
email_queue
media_queue
voting_queue
audit_queue


============================================================
8. DEVOPS STANDARDS (K3s + HELM)
============================================================

DEPLOYMENT RULES
----------------
One Helm chart per service
Use values.yaml for configuration
Secrets stored in sealed-secrets
Horizontal scaling for API & workers

LOGGING
-------
Structured JSON logs
Include request_id
Include user_id when available

MONITORING
----------
Health checks for API, workers, DB
Prometheus metrics
Grafana dashboards


============================================================
9. SECURITY STANDARDS
============================================================

AUTHENTICATION
--------------
JWT tokens in httpOnly cookies
No tokens in localStorage

INPUT VALIDATION
----------------
Validate all inputs server-side
Sanitize HTML inputs
Limit file upload size

AUTHORIZATION
-------------
RoleGuard on frontend
RBAC middleware on backend
Audit log for admin actions


============================================================
10. GIT & CI/CD STANDARDS
============================================================

BRANCHING
---------
main: production
develop: staging
feature/*: new features
hotfix/*: urgent fixes

COMMITS
-------
feat: new feature
fix: bug fix
docs: documentation
refactor: code cleanup
test: testing
chore: misc

PULL REQUESTS
-------------
Must include description
Must include screenshots for UI changes
Must pass linting & tests
Must be reviewed by 1+ developers


============================================================
11. TESTING STANDARDS
============================================================

FRONTEND
--------
Unit tests: UI components
Integration tests: hooks + API
E2E tests: pages + routing

BACKEND
-------
Unit tests: services
Integration tests: routers + DB
Load tests: events, voting, media


============================================================
12. DOCUMENTATION STANDARDS
============================================================
Every feature must include:
- README.md
- API endpoints
- Component list
- Data models
- User flows